cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize this numerical solver or benchmark methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "Parallel Heat Diffusion Simulation on Large 2D/3D Grids (MPI + OpenMP)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
url: "https://github.com/SidhartSami/pdc-heat-diffusion"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SidhartSami/pdc-heat-diffusion"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sami"
    given-names: "Sidhart"
    orcid: ""
  - family-names: "Rafy"
    given-names: "Abdul"
    affiliation: "FAST-NUCES"
abstract: >-
  A high-performance, distributed-memory (MPI) and shared-memory (OpenMP) numerical solver
  for 2D and 3D transient heat diffusion using an explicit FTCS finite-difference scheme.
  Features Cartesian topology decomposition, non-blocking compute-communication overlap,
  NUMA-aware first-touch initialization, L2 cache spatial blocking, parallel VTK output,
  and bit-exact checkpoint/restart mechanisms.
keywords:
  - "parallel computing"
  - "distributed memory"
  - "MPI"
  - "OpenMP"
  - "heat equation"
  - "stencil computation"
  - "domain decomposition"
  - "FTCS"
  - "cache blocking"
license: "MIT"
